===AFTER===
defmodule Solution do
  def build_groups(acc, []) do
    [Enum.reverse(acc)]
  end

  def build_groups([head | _] = acc, [next | rest]) do
    if next == head + 1 do
      build_groups([next | acc], rest)
    else
      [Enum.reverse(acc) | build_groups([next], rest)]
    end
  end
end
===ASSUMPTIONS===
proper_lists
===RATIONALE===
`acc ++ [next]` is O(n) per append in a recursive accumulator — replace with prepend `[next | acc]` and a single `Enum.reverse/1` at the end; also drops the O(n) `List.last/1` by matching the head.
